From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Faizal <sahil.faizal@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] hip-tests: Give outputs one writer and read CAS state atomically

The comprehensive CSAN HIP tests report duplicate device writes in test
kernels and plain initial reads racing with atomicCAS updates. Preserve
all collective participants, assign each output to one thread, and use
an atomic initial load at the matching agent or system scope.

Use grid-stride work for callbacks, launch-bound and symbol-copy kernels,
restrict collective-result stores to their designated leaders, and check
every bfloat16 lane independently. Preserve every deliberate delay-loop
store in addCountReverse while correcting its shadowed output index.

Source: ROCm/rocm-systems bd1130f9f838cfffd24f41fd3052968fb7cae4e0
Reproduction: https://github.com/ROCm/TheRock/actions/runs/43015193286
Validation: source-derived CPU ownership/value controls reproduce the
baseline overlaps and pass after these changes. The actual extracted CAS
helper reproduces a host CSAN race before the fix and passes with four
threads at agent and system scope for all three integer types afterward.
The actual artifact compiler accepts all eleven modified full translation
units and representative consumers of both headers for gfx942 host/device
compilation; GPU execution remains pending. No instrumentation is disabled.
Carry temporarily in TheRock pending upstream HIP-test review.
